1
00:00:36,640 --> 00:00:44,620
CONVERSATION 1
Today's special guest is Lord Blackwell, one of our country's most experienced and distinguished career diplomats.

2
00:00:44,620 --> 00:00:45,640
Welcome!

3
00:00:45,640 --> 00:00:47,300
It's my pleasure.

4
00:00:47,300 --> 00:00:52,560
Our audience will be most interested in learning about a career in the foreign service.

5
00:00:52,560 --> 00:01:01,800
However, before we talk about that, I'd like to ask you about the current developments hitting the news today regarding the Republic of Winopia.

6
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:03,400
What can you tell us?

7
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:07,460
I'm afraid I don't know much beyond what we've all seen on the news.

8
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:19,680
It looks like the government of Winopia seems to be undergoing some sort of crisis of legitimacy, and an interim administration has been transitionally established until a head of state is agreed on.

9
00:01:19,680 --> 00:01:30,080
But my career work has mostly focused around the continental spheres of Europe and the Americas, and thus I've never been involved with Winopian relations.

10
00:01:30,080 --> 00:01:36,140
It's for this reason that I don't know anything on this matter beyond what we can all read in the newspapers.

11
00:01:36,140 --> 00:01:37,620
Oh, I see.

12
00:01:37,620 --> 00:01:50,320
Nevertheless, be rest assured that our expert envoys at our consulate there will be closely monitoring the situation, and I expect our bilateral relations with that country will not be affected.

13
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:53,540
So how does one get a career in foreign relations?

14
00:01:53,540 --> 00:01:57,080
There are many different paths one can take.

15
00:01:57,080 --> 00:01:59,160
All diplomats have their own story.

16
00:01:59,160 --> 00:02:06,180
But in my case, I got a degree in electrical engineering followed by six years' service in the air force.

17
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:14,580
Then I went to law school, and upon obtaining a degree in international law, I joined the diplomatic corps where I have been for 22 years.

18
00:02:14,580 --> 00:02:18,320
What would you say are the key skills one needs for the job?

19
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:20,620
There are so many.

20
00:02:20,620 --> 00:02:23,560
Being a hard worker and a good student is important.

21
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:25,060
You never stop learning.

22
00:02:25,060 --> 00:02:30,020
In addition, a diplomat needs to be very articulate in their discourse and rhetoric.

23
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:42,500
Whether it is defusing attention or enacting policy, people and communication skills are vital.

24
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:59,980
Q1. What do we learn about the man from the conversation?

25
00:02:59,980 --> 00:03:18,940
