00:03:57,200 --> 00:04:01,280
CONVERSATION 2
It's getting late and we're both displaying signs of weariness.

29
00:04:01,280 --> 00:04:04,100
I think we should call it a day and meet again tomorrow morning.

30
00:04:04,100 --> 00:04:05,480
Oh, come on, Jeff.

31
00:04:05,480 --> 00:04:07,000
We are so close!

32
00:04:07,000 --> 00:04:08,940
Don't you think we are almost done?

33
00:04:08,940 --> 00:04:11,900
Let's do two more hours, please.

34
00:04:11,900 --> 00:04:14,400
One hour, then I'm going home.

35
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:15,120
OK, fine.

36
00:04:15,120 --> 00:04:21,680
I think we are making good progress, and that with a few more amendments, we will be all done.

37
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:23,640
I'm sure looking forward to it.

38
00:04:23,640 --> 00:04:25,780
I'm so tired of this project.

39
00:04:25,780 --> 00:04:27,100
Don't get me wrong.

40
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:33,280
It's a great professional opportunity for me and a milestone for the company, but it's just been so long.

41
00:04:33,280 --> 00:04:34,540
Yeah.

42
00:04:34,540 --> 00:04:38,900
Two months working on nothing but the same contract is a little tough.

43
00:04:38,900 --> 00:04:43,660
Nevertheless, I think that with a bit of luck, we'll be done by next week.

44
00:04:43,660 --> 00:04:46,120
Ha, you must be delusional.

45
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:47,480
You don't think so?

46
00:04:47,480 --> 00:04:49,160
No chance.

47
00:04:49,160 --> 00:04:54,240
Sections 4, 5, 8 and 9 still have to be aligned to the new framework.

48
00:04:54,240 --> 00:04:59,760
Then we need to proofread the whole thing and make sure all selling points are watertight.

49
00:04:59,760 --> 00:05:02,520
But that will all take no more than a couple of days.

50
00:05:02,520 --> 00:05:04,520
I wasn't finished.

51
00:05:04,520 --> 00:05:08,820
When we are done with it and send it upstairs, what do you think will happen?

52
00:05:08,820 --> 00:05:09,440
What?

53
00:05:09,440 --> 00:05:12,180
They'll argue about it for like a month.

54
00:05:12,180 --> 00:05:17,520
There's always going to be the odd board member who intervenes and demands rectifications be made.

55
00:05:17,520 --> 00:05:22,220
They might think that being helpful, but in reality that being obstructive and hampering progress.

56
00:05:22,220 --> 00:05:26,320
Oh, Jeff, you're too preoccupied and cynical.

57
00:05:26,320 --> 00:05:28,180
It won't be anywhere as bad as that.

58
00:05:28,180 --> 00:05:38,980
You'll see, the entire managerial hierarchy wants to see this project implemented as soon as possible, and the board, too, is virtually unanimous in its support.

59
00:05:38,980 --> 00:05:50,420
Go on then, let's stop there and meet up again same time tomorrow.

60
00:05:50,420 --> 00:06:07,300
Q5. Why does the man suggest they call it a day?

